casebook inert-claim-fixture v1
source "deliberately defective fixture for pass 6" dated 2026-09-22 by "quorum tests"
note "A claim that cannot reach any action. cbc must SAY SO."
note ""
note "This is the defect pass 6 was added to catch, reduced to its smallest form. `bearing_failing` is supported,"
note "is attacked, holds in real states -- and attacks nothing, so no state of the world in which it is true can"
note "ever change what the machine does. It reads in review as though the hazard is handled. It is not."
note ""
note "Found for real in tank-409, where `level_safe` had exactly this shape, and its absence meant the casebook"
note "continued a transfer on 'nothing said stop' rather than on 'something said safe'."

observe vib_high    "casing vibration above the alarm limit"
observe temp_high   "bearing temperature above the alarm limit"
observe just_serviced "the bearing was replaced this shift"

# This one is wired up properly.
claim overheating "the bearing is running hot" needs temp_high

# This one is not. Supported, defeasible, and inert.
claim bearing_failing "the bearing is failing" needs vib_high
just_serviced rebuts bearing_failing

action stop    safe when overheating
action monitor idle
prefer stop over monitor
